 "answer": "Johor Bahru's air quality is **Unhealthy** at the moment, based on the most recent reading I found. I can't pull a live feed, so these figures come from search results and may be a little out of date.\n\n- **Latest reading:** The US AQI is 180 (Unhealthy), with PM2.5 at 111 µg/m³ and PM10 at 151 µg/m³. That was last updated on 2026-10-16 at 15:51 local time.\n- **Other sources:** One Malaysia-focused tracker lists Johor Bahru as Unhealthy, with a 24-hour average PM2.5 of about 136.8 µg/m³. That is roughly US AQI 212, or Very Unhealthy, but it's an estimate, and the page flags the data as stale. Another aggregator shows Johor Bahru at an Unhealthy 166.\n- **Older reading:** An IQAir page showed a Moderate reading of 62, but it appears to be an old snapshot, so I wouldn't rely on it.\n\nThe sources don't agree exactly, but most point to unhealthy air. At that level, everyone can start to feel effects, and sensitive groups can be affected more seriously. It's sensible to:\n- limit prolonged outdoor exertion\n- wear an N95 or KN95 mask outdoors\n- keep windows closed\n- use an air purifier indoors if you have one\n\nFor the official number, check the Malaysian Department of Environment's API (Air Pollutant Index) or the IQAir page for Johor Bahru.",
